Instead of wandering around for new discoveries along the boardwalk, you decide to relax and enjoy the scenery.  Walking over to the railing, you place your elbows onto the weathered wooden railing and rest your head in your hands. You watch as the rhythmic, low rumble of the tide rolls in. It washes over the sand, turning to foam as it does so, and drowns out the ambient chatter of the crowd behind you. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightGreen">A soft breeze blows over you, bringing the smell of salt and a faint fish smell. Closing your eyes, you savor the feeling of the cool breeze on your face. Opening your eyes again, you return your attention to the water. It’s a peaceful, mesmerizing view, despite the bustling stream of tourists eating ice cream and snapping photos just a few feet away.</span> <br>
<br>
