    <span style="color:Yellow">You brace yourself for the inevitable pointing, laughing, or even a gasp from someone on the boardwalk.</span> Slowly, agonizingly, you glance to your left. The family is still looking over the map, and not at you. You look to your right. An elderly couple is intently focused on eating their ice cream cones. In front of you, a group of teenagers walk past, completely absorbed in their phones. Miraculously, no one is looking at you. The people are entirely wrapped up in their own worlds. You let out a breath you didn’t realize you were holding, your shoulders dropping an inch. The adrenaline begins to fade and the heat in your cheeks starts to cool. <br>
